    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0389" n="879" sameAs="frus:frus1948v01p2/pg879"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.AL/2–2748: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in the United
                        Kingdom </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-02-28T12:00:00-05:00">February 28,
                            1948—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>690. For Douglas from Clayton and Thorp. Re urtel 726. Feb 25. Dept completely in
                    accord with position stated and action recommended Habana tel 249, Feb 27
                    repeated to London. Pls proceed discussions with British officials on basis
                    indicated last paragraph Habana tel 249. We leave presentation this position to
                    your judgment.</p>
                <pb facs="0390" n="880" xml:id="pg880"/>
                <p>We are anxious that presentation be made in manner best calculated to avoid
                    antagonism and to minimize effect on our cooperation with British on other
                    issues. Sent London as 690, repeated Habana as 275. [Clayton and Thorp.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
